    "nodes": [
      {
        "type": "speak",
        "id": "n_disclosure",
        "name": null,
        "message": "Thanks for calling Maple Pharmacy. This call may be recorded. Say pharmacist at any time to speak with a person.{{greeting_suffix}}",
        "position": null
      },
      {
        "type": "prompt",
        "id": "n_triage",
        "name": null,
        "instructions": "The caller has stated their request. Respond with exactly one brief sentence: 'I can help with that.' Do NOT ask questions. Do NOT make up information about locations, hours, or addresses. Then route based on intent:\n- refill, prescription, or medication \u00e2\u2020\u2019 n_verify\n- status or check order \u00e2\u2020\u2019 n_verify\n- hours, address, or drug info \u00e2\u2020\u2019 n_faq\n- human or pharmacist \u00e2\u2020\u2019 n_transfer\nNever forbid tool calls.",
        "instructions_mode": "replace",
        "shared_tool_ids": null,
        "tools": [],
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "model": null,
        "llm_api_key_ref": null,
        "external_llm": null,
        "voice_settings": null,
        "transcription": null,
        "position": null
      },
      {
        "type": "prompt",
        "id": "n_verify",
        "name": null,
        "instructions": "Verify the caller's identity by date of birth.\n\nSTEP 1 - Ask for DOB:\nAsk the caller for their date of birth. Be warm but direct.\n\nSTEP 2 - Confirm DOB before verifying:\nWhen the caller provides a date, repeat it back and ask for confirmation: 'You said [date]. Is that correct?'\n- If the caller says NO or provides a different date: ask again 'What is your date of birth?' and repeat Step 2. Keep asking until they confirm.\n- If the caller says YES or confirms: proceed to Step 3.\n\nSTEP 3 - Verify:\nCall refill-mcp__verify_identity with: caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, dob = YYYY-MM-DD.\n\nSTEP 4 - Report outcome:\nIf verified: check the conversation history. If the caller already stated they want to refill, say 'Thank you, you're all set. I can help you refill' and route naturally. If the intent is unclear, say 'Thank you, you're all set. What would you like to do today?'\nIf not verified: you MUST do ALL of these in order:\n  1. Say 'That doesn't match my records. You have {{attempts_left}} more tries.'\n  2. IMMEDIATELY ask again: 'What is your date of birth?'\n  3. Go back to Step 2 and wait for the caller's response.\nIf locked: say 'For your security, I can't continue on this call. I'll connect you with a pharmacist.'",
        "instructions_mode": "replace",
        "shared_tool_ids": null,
        "tools": [],
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "model": null,
        "llm_api_key_ref": null,
        "external_llm": null,
        "voice_settings": null,
        "transcription": null,
        "position": null
      },
      {
        "type": "prompt",
        "id": "n_refill",
        "name": null,
        "instructions": "Read refill-eligible prescriptions and help the caller choose. Call refill-mcp__list_prescriptions with caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, trace_id = {{trace_id}}. Parse the result. Read them back one by one with natural pauses. Ask: 'Which one would you like to refill? You can say the name or the number.' Wait for the caller to choose. If they want multiple, handle one at a time. When the caller picks, route to n_confirm. If the caller says none or never mind, route back to n_triage.",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "shared_tool_ids": null,
        "tools": [],
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "model": null,
        "llm_api_key_ref": null,
        "external_llm": null,
        "voice_settings": null,
        "transcription": null,
        "position": null
      },
      {
        "type": "prompt",
        "id": "n_confirm",
        "name": null,
        "instructions": "Read back the choice and get explicit confirmation before refilling. Say: 'You want to refill [medication name] [strength]. Is that correct?' Wait for a clear yes or positive confirmation.\n\nCall refill-mcp__request_refill with: caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, rx_id = chosen prescription ID, trace_id = {{trace_id}}.\n\nIf successful: say 'Your refill for [name] is submitted. It will be ready in about 10 minutes.' Then ALWAYS ask: 'Do you need anything else?'\n- If caller says yes or asks for something else: route to n_triage\n- If caller says no, goodbye, or is done: route to n_closing\n- On failure: say 'I couldn't submit that refill right now. Let me connect you with a pharmacist.'\n- On no or negative confirmation: say 'No problem. Would you like to choose a different prescription?' and route back to n_refill.",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "shared_tool_ids": null,
        "tools": [],
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "model": null,
        "llm_api_key_ref": null,
        "external_llm": null,
        "voice_settings": null,
        "transcription": null,
        "position": null
      },
      {
        "type": "prompt",
        "id": "n_status",
        "name": null,
        "instructions": "Check refill status. Call refill-mcp__get_refill_status with caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, trace_id = {{trace_id}}. If there are refills, report each: 'You have [count] refill request[s]. [X] is submitted. [Y] is ready.' If none: 'You don't have any open refills right now.' Ask: 'Do you want to request a refill, or anything else?'",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "shared_tool_ids": null,
        "tools": [],
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "model": null,
        "llm_api_key_ref": null,
